**Selling Application:** Every client interaction, every piece of content, every product touchpoint is a memory event. If you don't engineer the review schedule, the client's memory of your value decays to near-zero within 31 days. The `reviewAt` field in `MemoryResidue` should be set using this formula. High-stability lessons (those that survived multiple reviews) should be weighted more heavily in future artifact generation.

```ts
// MemoryDecayScore = R(t) = e^(-daysSinceLastTouch / stability)
// If R(t) < 0.5, the client has forgotten more than they remember
const retention = Math.exp(-daysSinceLastTouch / memoryStability)
if (retention < 0.5) trigger("Re-engagement sequence. Memory below 50% retention.")
if (retention < 0.2) trigger("Emergency re-anchor. Client has effectively forgotten you.")
```

